  "family": "jazz",
  "lineage": "Polish alternative jazz movement of the 1990s centred on Gdańsk and the Tri-City and on the Bydgoszcz club Mózg, whose musicians adopted the deliberately skewed name yass to set themselves against the established jazz mainstream. Bands such as Miłość, with Tymon Tymański, Leszek Możdżer and Mikołaj Trzaska, as well as Kury and Łoskot, mixed free jazz with punk, rock, noise and ironic quotation of Polish popular music.",
